aarch64: define PAGE_SHIFT_CONST for the userspace kext tools.

kext.subproj/cross_link.c is compiled with -DKERNEL, so on arm64 mach/arm/vm_param.h
declares PAGE_SHIFT_CONST as extern int (arm64 chooses 4K/16K at kernel init) rather
than the compile-time 12 it is on i386/x86_64. Nothing in userspace defines it, so
IOKit_dylib failed to link (getEffectivePageSize / roundPageCrossSafe*). Provide the
definition here for arm64, fixed at 12 (4K) to match the host kernel-emulation shim
(ciderd xnu_sys_rs_shims.c also uses 12). Inert on x86, where the value is a macro.
--- a/kext.subproj/cross_link.c
+++ b/kext.subproj/cross_link.c
@@ -22,6 +22,14 @@
  */
 #include "cross_link.h"
 
+/* On ARM64, PAGE_SHIFT_CONST is declared as extern int in kernel headers.
+ * This file is compiled with -DKERNEL, so we need to provide the definition.
+ * Darling uses 4KB pages (PAGE_SHIFT = 12), matching the host kernel-emulation
+ * shim (ciderd xnu_sys_rs_shims.c). */
+#if defined(__aarch64__) || defined(__arm64__)
+int PAGE_SHIFT_CONST = 12;
+#endif
+
 
